---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Editorial Policy | HomeFixWise";
const description =
  "Learn how HomeFixWise researches, reviews, updates, and corrects home-repair content.";
---

<Base {title} {description}>
  <section class="page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">EDITORIAL POLICY</p>

    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>

    <p>
      HomeFixWise aims to publish useful, clear, and responsible information
      for homeowners in the United States and Canada.
    </p>

    <h2>Research standards</h2>

    <p>
      We aim to use trustworthy sources such as government agencies,
      manufacturers, trade organizations, utility providers, building-code
      resources, and established industry references where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>Cost information</h2>

    <p>
      Repair and replacement costs can vary significantly. We present cost
      information as estimates or ranges and explain the factors that may affect
      the final price.
    </p>

    <h2>Safety review</h2>

    <p>
      Content involving electrical systems, natural gas, combustion,
      structural damage, major water intrusion, and similar hazards is written
      conservatively. We separate simple homeowner observations from work that
      should be performed by qualified professionals.
    </p>

    <h2>Updates</h2>

    <p>
      Articles may be reviewed and updated when prices, products, regulations,
      technology, or industry guidance change.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>

    <p>
      When a meaningful factual error is identified, we aim to correct it
      promptly. Readers can report potential errors through our
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial independence</h2>

    <p>
      Advertising relationships should not determine the conclusions of our
      editorial content. Sponsored or commercial relationships will be
      disclosed where applicable.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>